  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Campus visitor-directory precision",
    "overview": "The measured campus leads. Compact Manrope, a monochrome header, quiet controls and fine dividers carry forward the survey viewer's layout and type system. Sunlit terrain and source imagery provide the scene's character; outdoor overlays stay quiet and readable. This independent React app runs on port 5174; the progressive COPC survey remains independently available on port 5173.\n\nThe owner explicitly requested a white-and-black interface with persistent light/dark switching. This approved colour-system change is scoped to this app; the original blue survey viewer retains its own system.\n\nThis document records the shipped implementation in `src/App.jsx`, `src/replica.css`, `src/style.css`, `src/scene.js` and `src/reconstruction-layers.js`. It preserves the inherited typography, structure and component shapes while documenting the approved monochrome palette. The rejected fitted building has been replaced with scan-derived geometry. The authorized western-roof repair uses an aerial outline and texture with measured rim heights; its unobserved interior remains an estimate. Local parking surfaces and small measured-centre patches improve detail without claiming recovered occlusions. Original points remains the comparison for all added surface layers. This record does not imply user approval of a final visual comp or calibrated geometric accuracy.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Measured building geometry remains the visual reference.",
      "Pale continuous controls frame an available-height spatial scene.",
      "Inverted pressed states and explicit labels make inspection modes legible.",
      "Source distinctions remain visible alongside the reconstructed context."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Theme Boundary",
        "body": "Theme changes affect interface chrome only. Keep the measured building, terrain imagery and recorded thermal palette unchanged.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Measured Content",
        "body": "Keep the scan-derived building and Original points comparison available. Display colour corrections must remain reversible and must not edit source RGB.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "Quiet Depth",
        "body": "Use tone and separators for permanent structure; reserve stronger cast shadows for temporary help and feedback.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "Registered Capture",
        "body": "W/T/Z must keep the same eastern-array geometry, camera and target. Normal uses modelled photovoltaic materials; W/T/Z uses supplied recorded imagery. The southern array has no supplied camera captures.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the inherited Manrope, monochrome theme roles, component shapes and visible keyboard focus.",
      "Do keep Original points and Captured RGB available for comparison with display treatments.",
      "Do preserve full-compound coverage, parking and both solar clusters.",
      "Do preserve camera, target and geometry when switching registered eastern-array captures.",
      "Do disclose scan-derived approximation, source gaps, modelled context and thermal limits.",
      "Do keep the estimated roof disclosure visible in Merged surface and hide all added surface layers in Original points.",
      "Do retain labelled mobile controls and scrollable drawer access."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace the measured university with guessed architectural shapes.",
      "Don't treat interpolated surface detail, image-traced extent or thermal colours as calibrated measurement.",
      "Don't use source data colours as a general UI action palette.",
      "Don't multiply permanent cards or strong shadows where the system uses separators."
